1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
In this video, I will introduce you to the key needle animation function.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:14,000
In 2025.0, the key needle can be applied to various elements, such as colors, fabrics, panels, joints, fixed needles, and wind control devices,

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
to achieve natural transition animation at any time.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The original animation mode was changed to animation editor after this update,

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
which is convenient for everyone to make animation directly in the simulation mode.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
The overall usability has also been improved.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Click on the animation in the top menu, then select the animation editor to open it.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000
First, let's take a look at the animation editor layout after the update, and see how to set up the key needle.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
You can see that the tool bar at the top of the editor retains familiar options,

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
such as recording, playback, camera animation, and simulation quality.

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
In addition, the automatic key needle function has been added,

12
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
and other settings related to the configuration have been moved to the configuration panel on the right.

13
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
On the left side of the editor,

14
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
the animation layer list will be set to the tree structure,

15
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
and the animation object in the scene will be displayed.

16
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,000
When applying animation, the costume, wind controller, and flag will appear as the object layer in the top layer.

17
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Click on the triangle next to each object to check the properties that can be animated.

18
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,000
These properties will be displayed as the property layer.

19
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,000
The name of the object layer cannot be edited directly in the animation editor,

20
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
but for some objects, you can rename them in the object window scene selection card.

21
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,000
To set up the key needle,

22
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
please click on the right side of the property layer to insert the key needle.

23
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,000
According to the different properties,

24
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,000
you can use the option box to start or stop using the property,

25
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
or enter the specific value to manually set up the key needle.

26
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The key needle will be displayed as a zero-shape icon,

27
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,000
easy to identify.

28
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,000
The animation track in the middle of the screen will be adjusted to display the animation range of each object,

29
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
helping you to clearly control the animation time and space.

30
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Animated animation based on simulation storage,

31
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
such as costume or software model animation,

32
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,000
will be displayed as red,

33
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
while key needle animation will be displayed as gray.

34
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Click on the animation button on the top left side

35
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
to open a list of objects that support animation,

36
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
including colors,

37
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
materials,

38
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,000
panels,

39
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,000
virtual models,

40
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
and cameras.

41
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,000
After selecting the object,

42
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
it will be added to the list of objects,

43
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
and you can apply the key needle for it.

44
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Next,

45
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:15,000
let's take a look at the time line area in the middle of the interface.

46
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
The curve line above the gray bar on the top of the top part

47
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,000
indicates the range of play.

48
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
It defines the part that will be played in the animation.

49
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
You can adjust the range of play in the following ways.

50
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Drag both ends,

51
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
directly drag the two ends of the gray bar,

52
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,000
drag the entire time axis,

53
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
press the mouse button to drag the entire gray bar,

54
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
and you can move the play range.

55
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
The key needle and end needle after adjustment

56
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
will also be implemented in the configuration panel.

57
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
You can also directly enter values ​​in the configuration panel

58
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
to set them.

59
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Click on the right arrow on the time axis,

60
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,000
you can choose to set the starting or ending needle,

61
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:53,000
and set the current needle as the starting or end point of the play range.

62
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Choose to limit the range in the action needle,

63
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
the play range will automatically adjust to the position of all existing key needles.

64
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,000
In addition,

65
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:06,000
you can press the Ctrl key and roll the mouse wheel to search for the size of the time axis,

66
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
so that you can check the range of the needle more carefully.

67
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:13,000
The time axis slider at the bottom allows you to set the range of the needle.

68
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Click on the right arrow in the slider area,

69
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
there will be three options.

70
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Choose to configure the action needle,

71
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
the time axis will automatically adjust to all animation layers,

72
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
and the range between the first and last key needle in the animation layer.

73
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
To configure the play range,

74
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:30,000
adjust the test picture according to the currently defined play range.

75
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
To configure all needles,

76
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
adjust the test picture according to the current time axis

77
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
with the smallest and largest needles set at both ends of the slider.

78
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:42,000
You can also directly click on the button on the right side of the input frame of the end needle to complete this operation.

79
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,000
The configuration panel on the right allows you to control some general play settings,

80
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
such as the time axis range,

81
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
scene time curve and display units.

82
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Two new options have been added,

83
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
the real time and save time.

84
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,000
The real time,

85
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
which is often referred to as FPS,

86
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
it defines the rate of play per second.

87
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,000
The higher the real time,

88
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
the smoother the animation playback,

89
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,000
but it will also increase the rendering time and file size.

90
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
You can choose the right real time according to the needs of the project,

91
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
to balance quality and performance.

92
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Save time,

93
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:15,000
control how to deal with the key needle when changing the real time.

94
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
When this option is closed,

95
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
the total play time will remain unchanged,

96
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:23,000
but the real time of the key needle will be adjusted according to the new real time per second.

97
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
When this option is turned on,

98
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
the real time of the key needle will remain unchanged,

99
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
and the total play time will be adjusted according to the new real time per second.

100
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Through these new functions,

101
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,000
you can more flexibly control the range and speed of animation playback,

102
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
and optimize your workflow.

103
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Now let's learn how to create and edit animation.

104
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,000
For save animation based on simulation,

105
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
such as clothing or software models,

106
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
you can continue to use the record button as before.

107
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
In the 2025 version,

108
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
we added the function of cutting and merging animation layers.

109
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,000
In the past,

110
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
we often needed to go through the third-party software

111
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,000
to edit and record the good animation layers.

112
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Now,

113
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
you can freely cut or merge them according to your needs.

114
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,000
To cut a layer,

115
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
right-click on the layer you want to cut,

116
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
then select the cut layer.

117
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
The layer will be cut in the current real time,

118
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:16,000
and the chip will appear directly in the track above the original layer.

119
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
To merge multiple layers,

120
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
press the Ctrl key,

121
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,000
and select the layer you want to merge.

122
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Or use the Shift key to select continuously,

123
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
then right-click and select the merge layer.

124
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,000
When merging layers,

125
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
it will be the top layer as the standard.

126
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Because the current animation layer is cut and received,

127
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:35,000
so the effect between them is naturally continued.

128
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
If there is a overlap,

129
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
the higher-level data will be prioritized during the merging process.

130
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
We can also play and check the effect before merging the layer.

131
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
This is consistent with the effect after merging.

132
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,000
After confirming the effect,

133
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
merge layer operation is possible.

134
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
In the case of file storage animation,

135
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,000
it is different from the object listed in the animation menu.

136
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
It requires manual setting of keyframes,

137
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
so that the animation works.

138
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Let's look at every animation project,

139
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
and review how to set keyframes,

140
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,000
and other important things to note.

141
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,000
We will start from the color animation.

142
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
There are two ways to set keyframes,

143
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,000
use the add animation button in the layer table.

144
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Set directly from the editor

145
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
or attribute editor of the object.

146
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Click on the add animation button.

147
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Select the color.

148
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Create an empty flag layer, then click on the triangle on the left

149
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Open layer, check its properties

150
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:27,000
In the drop-down menu, you can see the flag list that can be used for clothing

151
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:32,000
The content of the flag list display will be updated in real time according to the flag in the flag editor

152
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Now, we first add a key pin for the white flag

153
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,000
The first key pin will appear on the first pin in the hidden layer

154
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
The key pin is based on the setting of the current pin

155
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,000
You can directly move the head to the target pin

156
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Then select the flag color and click to insert the key pin

157
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Or enter the number of pins in the current pin input frame

158
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:55,000
It's the same, select the flag color and click to insert the key pin

159
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
To check whether the key pin has been added correctly

160
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
You can use the arrow buttons on the left and right sides of the key pin

161
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:05,000
They can make you quickly jump between the existing key pins

162
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:09,000
After confirming that the key pin is in place, return to the first pin and click the play button

163
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
You will see the flag color smooth

164
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:15,000
The natural animation effect is presented by the set key pin

165
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Now let's see how to add the key pin directly from the flag editor

166
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Move to the position you want to add the key pin

167
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Select a flag color and then click to insert the key pin in the upper right corner of the editor

168
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:34,000
After adding the key pin, you can drag the two ends of the object layer to adjust the overall length

169
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:36,000
At the same time, keep the relative distance between them

170
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:40,000
You can also drag the entire layer to move all key pins at once

171
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Or press and drag each key pin to a new position to adjust its position

172
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:50,000
You can select multiple key pins together by clicking or pressing Shift

173
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:54,000
And as a group of movements, keep them relative

174
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:59,000
To delete a specific key pin, please press and drag each key pin to select multiple key pins

175
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,000
Then right-click and select Delete Key Pin

176
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Or press the Delete key on the keyboard to delete the key pin

177
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
If the animation layer is too much to slow down the playback

178
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
You can click the eye icon on the left side

179
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,000
Activate or turn off the playback of one animation

180
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Let's just play it and see the current speed

181
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Now cut back to the first pin

182
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
Turn off the animation of the flag color

183
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:26,000
You can see that after turning off the flag color animation layer

184
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
The playback speed of the animation is obviously faster

185
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
If you want to delete the animation layer

186
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Please right-click on the layer in the list

187
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Then select Delete Layer

188
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Since the layer uses a tree structure

189
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:40,000
Therefore, deleting the object layer will also delete the related attribute layer

190
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
If you accidentally delete the attribute layer

191
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:46,000
You can right-click on the object layer and select

192
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Increase layer to re-add

193
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
You will see a list of movable attributes

194
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
And you can choose the attribute to be added separately

195
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Now let's see how to create a virtual model animation

196
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Including using the joint point to adjust the posture and set the key pin

197
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Click the Increase Animation button

198
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
The mouse will stop on the virtual model list

199
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:10,000
At this time, the virtual model list added in the current scene will appear

200
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Click the virtual model you need

201
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Add it to the layer list

202
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Click the triangle to open and check its attribute layer

203
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
To add the current position as the first key pin

204
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Please set the current pin as 0 first

205
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Then click the key pin button on the right side to set the key pin

206
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Press the Shift and X keys on the keyboard

207
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:32,000
You can display the virtual model's joint point in the 3D window

208
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Next, move the playback head to change the position of the pin

209
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
Adjust the joint point to modify the posture

210
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Then click the key pin button on the right side of the joint layer to insert the key pin button

211
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Set another key pin

212
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Because virtual model animation usually needs to be repeated

213
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,000
The steps of moving the pin, adjusting the position and inserting the key pin

214
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Therefore, the automatic key pin function will be more efficient

215
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,000
You can insert the key pin manually in the first pin

216
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Open the automatic key pin

217
00:09:56,000 --> 00:10:00,000
In this way, any subsequent joint adjustment will automatically generate the key pin

218
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
If the pin already has a key pin

219
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:05,000
The new position will cover the existing key pin

220
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Now the virtual model's posture is roughly edited

221
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Let's cut back to the first pin first

222
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
To confirm the animation effect

223
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
After confirming the current effect

224
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,000
You can also copy and paste the key pin

225
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Click or drag to select one or more key pins

226
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Right-click and select Copy Key Pin

227
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Or press Ctrl and C on the keyboard

228
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
Move the playback head to the pin to be pasted

229
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Then right-click and select Paste Key Pin

230
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Or press Ctrl and V

231
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
The key pin will be pasted on the current pin

232
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
If you paste multiple key pins

233
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
It will also keep the original pin

234
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
Now let's play it again

235
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:46,000
Check the animation effect after pasting the key pin

236
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:49,000
You can also right-click on the object layer

237
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,000
And use it in the right-click menu

238
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Adjust the joint pin and move to the ground function

239
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:00,000
In addition, you can also download and modify the existing MTN file

240
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:04,000
But in order to avoid remodeling in the current scene

241
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Please open the file in the new window

242
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Now let's see how to set the animation for the board

243
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
By adding a key pin

244
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,000
You can control the change of the material on the selected board at any time

245
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,000
To create animation

246
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
After selecting the board

247
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,000
You can increase the animation by pressing the animation button

248
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
But for the board

249
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:27,000
It is usually more efficient to insert the key pin directly from the property editor

250
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
First, the position where the key pin needs to be added is set

251
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
This place has been set as the hand pin

252
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Then select the board with the animation effect to be increased

253
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
In the property editor

254
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Select the material for the board to be used

255
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
